message: If you use dirk in your work, please cite it as below.
title: "dirk: a terminal multiplexer that knows what its sessions are for"
abstract: >-
  A terminal multiplexer whose sidebar is the product: a clickable project tree,
  static layouts, real coding-agent lifecycle states, and workspaces named from
  what the program inside them says it is doing.
